<article class="env-example" id="062Q">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/062Q">Example <span data-tag="062Q">9.2.2.20</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{QCat}$ denote the full subcategory of $\operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}$ spanned by the $\infty $-categories, and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}= \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{hc}}( \operatorname{QCat})$ be its homotopy coherent nerve (see Construction <a data-tag="0209" href="/tag/0209">5.5.3.1</a>). Then the inclusion functor </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(\operatorname{QCat}) \hookrightarrow \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{hc}}( \operatorname{QCat}) = \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}} \]
</div>
<p> is finitary: this follows by combining Corollary <a data-tag="039G" href="/tag/039G">9.2.1.13</a> with Corollary <a data-tag="03DG" href="/tag/03DG">9.1.6.3</a>. More generally, if $\lambda $ is an uncountable regular cardinal and $\operatorname{QCat}_{&lt; \lambda }$ denote the category of $\lambda $-small $\infty $-categories, then the inclusion functor $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{QCat}_{&lt; \lambda } ) \hookrightarrow \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{hc}}( \operatorname{QCat}_{&lt; \lambda } ) = \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{&lt; \lambda } )$ is $(\aleph _0, \lambda )$-finitary. </p>
</article>
